# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  SECURITY: this project drives real, signed-in financial accounts.
#  Everything below can contain private data or live sessions. Never commit it.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Live browser sessions (cookies / auth tokens) — the most dangerous leak
*browser-profile/
browser-profile/
**/*browser-profile*/

# Real per-account config (KEEP the sanitized example)
config.json
config.*.json
!config.example.json

# Downloaded documents — your actual financial records
*.pdf
*.zip

# Runtime state / output
discovery.json
progress.json
# Whether the last listing was read whole, and when.
last-listing.json
panel-runs.json
# NetBenefits keeps the plans of a sign-in with several here, with the
# site's own plan and employer numbers in their addresses.
plans.json
new-this-run.txt
run-summary.txt
# ...and any hand-made copy of them. A file like "discovery.json.pre-fix" or
# "progress.json.bak" holds the same real account data as the original, but
# the exact-name rules above do not cover it - one was nearly committed while
# building a new app.
discovery.json.*
progress.json.*
plans.json.*
# Same reasoning for config: a "config.json.save" or "config.json.bak" holds
# the owner name and local output paths just as the original does. The
# example stays allowed by the rule above.
config.json.*
!config.example.json
*.json.bak
*.json.orig
*.csv.bak
*.log
*.csv

# Output / working folders created by the tools
**/Statements/
**/Pay Statements/
**/Tax Documents/
**/Year-End Summaries/
**/Manual Review/
**/Trade Confirmations/
**/Insurance Documents/
**/EOBs/
**/Plan Documents/
**/Authorizations/
**/Letters/
**/ID Cards/
**/Other Documents/
**/Receipts/
**/Orders/
**/In-Store/
**/Online/
**/App Store/
**/Apple Store/
**/Rides/
**/Uber Eats/
**/Logs/
**/Diagnostics/
**/Backups/

# Build artifacts (the core wheel is built on demand)
core/dist/
build/

# Python
# No trailing slash. Off Windows a worktree's .venv is a symlink, and a
# pattern ending in / matches only a real folder.
.venv
venv
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
# uv users lock locally, and gui/pyproject.toml is the shared list (#108)
gui/uv.lock
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Verizon browser download temp dir
**/.vz-downloads/

# The status dashboard lists which providers you hold accounts with, plus how
# current each archive is. It belongs next to your installs, never in the repo.
status.html
**/status.html
# spreadsheets the exporters write beside the installs, and the reader's cache
*Purchases.xlsx
*Purchases.csv
*Transactions.xlsx
*Transactions.csv
.transactions-cache.json

# build output
dist/

# Additional provider output stays private
**/Reports/

# Release working area: downloaded artifacts and the notes for a pending release
.release/

# A failing suite's whole pytest output, kept by tools/run_all_tests.py. It
# holds whatever a test printed, so it stays on the machine that ran it.
test-output/
